  "tiled_processing_discussion": {
    "status": "Proposed workflow; neighbour reconciliation is not implemented.",
    "approach": "Process independent sheets with a bounded worker queue, retain original edge contour and point constraints plus unknown-height selection/provenance, and re-interpolate shared neighbourhoods once adjacent sheets are available, including corner neighbours.",
    "overlap_limit": "At 30 m the directional search reaches 3.6 km; gradient paths and repeated refinement can propagate farther. This is not a validated sufficient overlap width. Validate with larger overlaps or rerun affected sheets with neighbouring context.",
    "constraints": "Keep measured point/contour heights distinct from inferred heights. Recompute unknown estimates with joint context. Raster blending alone does not resolve contradictory source labels.",
    "grid": "WGS84 sheet boundaries; shared reconciliation jobs require a common working grid, including when neighbours use different UTM zones."
  },
